nsides. This is useful for having buffers without having all the fluids being wasted.\n\n§2Here is an exmaple of a tank that will only output fluid once its full:§r\n\nFirstly, place a §6ROR Transmitter§r on one port of the tank, provide an ID and enable Polling.\n\n[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_Fluid1.png[/img]\n\nAfter that, place a §6ROR Logic Receiver§r next to the fluid valve and input the desired settings. Make sure that your signal is \u003e= of your desired buffer. One redstone level equals to 16k mb.\n\n[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_Fluid2.png[/img]\n\nA §3Fluid Control Pump§r can also be used to limit throughput of fluids and to also add priorities.",\n          "globalShare:1": 0,\n          "icon:10": {\n            "Count:3": 1,\n            "Damage:2": 0,\n            "OreDict:8": "",\n            "id:8": "hbm:tile.fluid_switch"\n          },\n          "isMain:1": 0,\n          "isSilent:1": 0,\n          "lockedProgress:1": 0,\n          "name:8": "Redstone Fluid Overflow",\n          "notification_duration:5": -1.0,\n          "notification_effect:3": -1,\n          "notification_fade_in:5": -1.0,\n          "notification_fade_out:5": -1.0,\n          "notification_icon_offset_y:3": -2147483648,\n          "notification_icon_scale:5": -1.0,\n          "notification_pos_x:3": -2147483648,\n          "notification_pos_y:3": -2147483648,\n          "notification_show_icon:8": "default",\n          "notification_style:8": "default",\n          "notification_subtitle:8": "",\n          "notification_subtitle_scale:5": -1.0,\n          "notification_title:8": "",\n          "notification_title_scale:5": -1.0,\n          "particle_count:3": -1,\n          "questLogic:8": "AND",\n          "repeatTime:3": -1,\n          "repeat_relative:1": 1,\n          "simultaneous:1": 0,\n          "snd_complete:8": "random.levelup",\n          "snd_update:8": "random.levelup",\n          "taskLogic:8": "OR",\n          "visibility:8": "NORMA